= Model selection bias — Simple =

'''Model selection bias''' happens when we try many models and pick the one with the best validation score partly because it got lucky on that particular validation data.

The more choices we try, the easier it is to accidentally optimize noise.

The winning validation score can then look better than the model's real future performance.

A separate final test set or nested cross-validation can help reduce this problem.

